{\pard\sb180\sa80\b\fs24 Injury\par}
{\pard\sa120 Mr. Robichaud is a 46-year-old underground scoop-tram operator at the Levack site. On February 11 he was thrown against the cab frame when the machine struck a muck pile. Diagnoses per Form 8 from Dr. Lyle Kowbel (Lockerby Family Health Team): right rotator cuff strain and mechanical low back pain. MRI of March 19 showed a partial-thickness supraspinatus tear and a small disc bulge at L4-L5, no nerve root contact. He reports a previous back strain in 2019, claim 29470116, fully resolved.\par}
{\pard\sb180\sa80\b\fs24 Treatment to date\par}
{\pard\sa120 Initial assessment Feb. 23, 2026. 15 visits attended, 2 missed (March 30, April 9 - highway closed). Manual therapy, progressive cuff and scapular strengthening, lumbar stabilization, HEP reviewed each visit. He takes naproxen 500 mg twice daily and stopped cyclobenzaprine on his own because of drowsiness.\par}
